India in 60 Seconds · History in 60 Seconds series · Silkscreen Travel Poster style

Picture: drawn in code (Canvas 2D). Print engine engine/silk.js from the Lemo-Opuscar library (MIT).
Landmarks (a brick city with a stepped bath and street drains, a stepped temple tower with a scholar and a slate of digits,
a domed marble tomb with minarets and a pool, a clock tower and arcade in the rain, walkers on a shore with salt heaps,
a sandstone fort wall under fireworks, a lander and rover on the Moon, a city with a metro and kites) are original stylised
silhouettes drawn as simple paths, not traced from photographs. No logos, no flags or emblems, no maps or borders.

Fonts (SIL Open Font License 1.1; licence texts in fonts/):
  Big Shoulders Display — Patric King / Google Fonts
  Outfit — Rodrigo Fuenzalida / Google Fonts

Voice: Kokoro-82M v1.0 (hexgrad, Apache-2.0) via kokoro-onnx, voice bm_george. Checked with faster-whisper (MIT), model base.en.

Music (original score, music/compose.py): sitar and tanpura by physical modelling (core/audio/pluck.py, Lemo-Opuscar, MIT);
tabla (dayan and bayan) synthesised in code. No samples.
Sound (mix.py): paper swish, stamps, a brush on paper, river, crickets, fountains, monsoon rain and thunder, surf, footsteps,
crowd, fireworks, radio beeps, city traffic: synthesised in code.
Mastering: FFmpeg (LGPL/GPL) via imageio-ffmpeg.

Facts and sources: FACTS.md.
